kavat-builtin-extensions.patch: the system's two extensions are part of the browser.

Kavat Browser loads two extensions of the system's, the Kavat one
(aelpfjkmocfiooliocnpmmbgcmbpjcne) and the blocker, uBlock Origin Lite
(ofdabgbaeilkjjdadjindcdlfonikhmo): the launcher passes them with
--load-extension, from a copy in the user's own folder. The blocker is a feature
of the browser that is always on, not a plugin that is turned on or off, and in
a private window more than anywhere. With this patch the two:

- work in private windows, as if "Allow in Incognito" were on, which cannot be
  turned off: ExtensionPrefs::IsIncognitoEnabled says yes for them, and
  everything that asks whether an extension runs in incognito (the requests the
  blocker's rules see, the scripts it puts in pages, its buttons on the toolbar)
  asks that in the end;
- cannot be turned off or removed, from chrome://extensions or by another
  extension: to the standard management policy they are as a component
  extension is, and they must remain installed;
- are not dropped when Enhanced Safe Browsing is on, which would otherwise
  ignore --load-extension.

They are not made component extensions, which would also need no launcher:
a component extension's static rule sets of declarativeNetRequest are never
loaded, because their checksums are only kept in the preferences when an
extension is installed (RulesMonitorService::OnExtensionLoaded), and their
index is written beside the extension, which in /usr cannot be written.

--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/extension_service.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/extension_service.cc
@@ -424,11 +424,8 @@
         << "--load-extension is not allowed in Google Chrome, ignoring.";
     return;
 #else   // BUILDFLAG(GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
-    if (safe_browsing::IsEnhancedProtectionEnabled(*profile_->GetPrefs())) {
-      VLOG(1) << "--load-extension is not allowed for users opted into "
-              << "Enhanced Safe Browsing, ignoring.";
-      return;
-    }
+    // Willwitcher-OS Kavat Edition: the system's two extensions come with this
+    // switch, so Enhanced Safe Browsing does not turn them off.
     if (ShouldBlockCommandLineExtension(*profile_)) {
       // TODO(crbug.com/401529219): Deprecate this restriction once
       // --load-extension removal on Chrome builds is fully launched.
--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/standard_management_policy_provider.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/standard_management_policy_provider.cc
@@ -29,6 +29,14 @@
 
 namespace {
 
+// Willwitcher-OS Kavat Edition: the system's two extensions, Kavat and the
+// blocker, are part of the browser: they cannot be turned off or removed, by
+// the user or by another extension.
+bool IsKavatSystemExtension(const Extension* extension) {
+  return extension->id() == "aelpfjkmocfiooliocnpmmbgcmbpjcne" ||
+         extension->id() == "ofdabgbaeilkjjdadjindcdlfonikhmo";
+}
+
 bool AdminPolicyIsModifiable(ExtensionManagement* settings,
                              const Extension* source_extension,
                              const Extension* extension,
@@ -74,6 +82,10 @@
     }
   }
 
+  if (IsKavatSystemExtension(extension)) {
+    is_modifiable = false;
+  }
+
   if (is_modifiable) {
     return true;
   }
@@ -296,6 +308,14 @@
 bool StandardManagementPolicyProvider::MustRemainInstalled(
     const Extension* extension,
     std::u16string* error) const {
+  if (IsKavatSystemExtension(extension)) {
+    if (error) {
+      *error = l10n_util::GetStringFUTF16(
+          IDS_EXTENSION_CANT_UNINSTALL_POLICY_REQUIRED,
+          base::UTF8ToUTF16(extension->name()));
+    }
+    return true;
+  }
   ManagedInstallationMode mode = settings_->GetInstallationMode(extension);
   // Disallow removing of recommended extension, to avoid re-install it
   // again while policy is reload. But disabling of recommended extension is
--- a/extensions/browser/extension_prefs.cc
+++ b/extensions/browser/extension_prefs.cc
@@ -1375,7 +1375,21 @@
   return false;
 }
 
+namespace {
+
+// Willwitcher-OS Kavat Edition: the system's two extensions, Kavat and the
+// blocker, are part of the browser and work in its private windows too.
+bool IsKavatSystemExtension(const ExtensionId& extension_id) {
+  return extension_id == "aelpfjkmocfiooliocnpmmbgcmbpjcne" ||
+         extension_id == "ofdabgbaeilkjjdadjindcdlfonikhmo";
+}
+
+}  // namespace
+
 bool ExtensionPrefs::IsIncognitoEnabled(const ExtensionId& extension_id) const {
+  if (IsKavatSystemExtension(extension_id)) {
+    return true;
+  }
   return ReadPrefAsBooleanAndReturn(extension_id, kPrefIncognitoEnabled);
 }
 
